// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
// Provenance: vendored from WebAssembly/wasi-cli, tag v0.2.0 (wit/stdio.wit).
//
// Vendored subset of the canonical WASI Preview 2 cli stdout
// interface.
//
// Source: WebAssembly/wasi-cli, tag v0.2.0
//   https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-cli/blob/v0.2.0/wit/stdio.wit
//
// Trimmed to the get-stdout() reader Capa's experimental --wasi mode
// imports (Stdio.print / Stdio.println -> get-stdout ->
// output-stream.blocking-write-and-flush loop). The upstream stdio.wit
// declares stdin / stdout / stderr in one file; here stdout and stderr
// are split into one file each (this file + stderr.wit) so each
// interface is independently greppable, and stdin is omitted because
// Stdio.read_line still travels the capa:host/stdio bridge (not yet
// migrated). All three interfaces belong to the same wasi:cli@0.2.0
// package as environment.wit; wasm-tools merges the package's .wit
// files when resolving deps/cli/.
//
// Canonical-ABI / unit conventions matching the host wasmtime
// add_wasip2() provides:
//   get-stdout -> output-stream : an OWNED output-stream handle the
//     guest writes the program's standard output to (via
//     output-stream.blocking-write-and-flush in <= 4096-byte chunks,
//     the one-OS-page bound a single blocking-write-and-flush honours),
//     then drops. The host renders / captures the bytes (in --wasi the
//     Capa host installs a WasiConfig stdout_custom callback that
//     accumulates them; see capa.runtime._wasm_component_host).
//
// The ``package wasi:cli@0.2.0;`` declaration lives ONLY in
// environment.wit (the first cli file): wasm-tools merges every .wit
// file in deps/cli/ into one package and rejects doc comments attached
// to more than one ``package`` item, so this file omits the package
// line and contributes only its interface to the shared package.

interface stdout {
  use wasi:io/streams@0.2.0.{output-stream};

  get-stdout: func() -> output-stream;
}
